Z||000000||bHooper||05-24-2000||10:49 PM||||when i went to pick up my Gt this afternoon, (had it aligned and emissions rejected).  they told me that i had a bad altenator.  this was a new one from Advance auto, and only had about 5 hours on it!<P>anyway, i replace the thing... reinstall the belt (note: i have never installed or adjusted a belt, ever... a friend did this for me originally) and went for a drive.<P>this is when the trouble started... when i would come to a stop sign, depress the clutch... the car would drop idle, and die!<P>did this happen because i have the belt improperly adjusted?  i also noticed that the car's temp. was 220 degrees.  is that ok? or is it a result of a improperly tightened belt?<P>i also noticed a lit tap tataptap from the engine compartment.  anybody... anybody... ?...?<P>thanks, for listening to me!<P>hoop||||reg||5
Z||000001||ROB MAC||05-25-2000||12:05 AM||||A loose belt will definitely cause a stalling condition and cause the water pump to operate improperly resulting in overheating. If the belt is real loose it might make that flapping or tapping noise. Get someone who knows to show you how tight it should be and how to secure it properly. If you continue to drive you'll kill the battery.||||reg||1
Z||000002||bHooper||05-25-2000||06:41 AM||||it seemed pretty tight to me... but then again i was pushing real hard with one hand and tightening with the wrench in the other.<P>hoop||||reg||1
Z||000003||bHooper||05-25-2000||08:49 AM||||well, i couldnt resist driveing the car into work today and... everything seemed normal.  the temp was around 220-230 at its highest and i never had a problem with the car dyeing!<P>maybe that was a result of haveing the battery disconected... maybe the ECM had to reset itself?<P>hoop||||reg||1
Z||000004||lennyb4||05-25-2000||11:57 AM||||As a general rule of thumb. A correctly tightened belt should have approx. 1/2" of movement when you push down on it.<P>just my .02*  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000005||theogre||05-25-2000||02:34 PM||||BH, any time you pull the battery the ECM will need to relearn everything.||||reg||1
